exports[`shows required options and positional arguments in command usage 1`] = `
"Usage: opencove space get [--space <id>] [options]

Get a space

When no target is given, inside OpenCove defaults to your own space; project options default to your own project.

Options:
  --space <id>    Select a space by its ID; also accepts @self, an exact name or a unique ID prefix (6+ characters) (required outside OpenCove)
  --project <id>  Narrow target lookup to a project; also accepts @self, an exact name or a unique ID prefix (6+ characters)

Table output (-o table): not supported.
Projectable fields: id, name, directoryPath, targetMountId, parentSpaceId, boundary, sortOrder, nodeIds, nodes, nodes.id, nodes.kind, nodes.title, nodes.projectId, nodes.spaceId, nodes.frame, nodes.frame.x, nodes.frame.y, nodes.frame.width, nodes.frame.height, nodes.status, nodes.sessionId, nodes.data, nodes.data.kind, nodes.data.status, nodes.data.priority, nodes.data.requirement, nodes.data.tags, nodes.data.url

Projection example:
  opencove space get --space s --fields id,nodes
  {"projectId":"p","activeSpaceId":"s","space":{"id":"s","nodes":[]}}

Examples:
  opencove space get --space space-123
  opencove space get --space space-123 --pretty

Global options: see "opencove --help".
"
`;
